questions.expected_answer:
Fixed code (use JSON.stringify when saving; handle possible null when parsing; map lat/lon to canvas coordinates):

<!doctype html>
<html>
  <body>
    <button id="saveBtn">Save Location</button>
    <canvas id="mapCanvas" width="400" height="200" style="border:1px solid #000"></canvas>

    <script>
      document.getElementById('saveBtn').addEventListener('click', saveLocation);

      function saveLocation() {
        navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(function(position) {
          var lat = position.coords.latitude;
          var lon = position.coords.longitude;

          // Save as a JSON string
          localStorage.setItem('coords', JSON.stringify({lat: lat, lon: lon}));

          // Read back and draw
          var stored = localStorage.getItem('coords');
          if (!stored) return; // nothing saved

          var coords = JSON.parse(stored);

          var canvas = document.getElementById('mapCanvas');
          var ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

          // Simple equirectangular mapping of lon/lat to canvas pixels
          var x = (coords.lon + 180) * (canvas.width / 360); // lon -180..180 -> 0..width
          var y = (90 - coords.lat) * (canvas.height / 180); // lat 90..-90 -> 0..height

          ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
          ctx.fillStyle = 'red';
          ctx.fillRect(x - 2.5, y - 2.5, 5, 5);
        }, function(err){
          alert('Geolocation error: ' + err.message);
        });
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

Explanation of the fix:
- Bug: localStorage.setItem expects a string. The original code stored a JS object directly, which becomes "[object Object]" and causes JSON.parse to throw.
- Fix: use JSON.stringify when saving and JSON.parse when reading.
- Added a null check after getItem to avoid parsing null.
- Improved drawing by mapping latitude/longitude into canvas pixel coordinates (so the dot appears on the canvas). Also cleared the canvas before drawing.

This ensures the coordinates are stored correctly and the red dot is drawn.

